$
\begin{array}{r}
\frac{\left[\mathrm{M}^{1} \mathrm{~L}^{2} \mathrm{~T}^{-2}\right]}{[\mathrm{\beta}]\left[\mathrm{L}^{1}\right]}=\left[\mathrm{M}^{0} \mathrm{~L}^{0} \mathrm{~T}^{0}\right] \\\\
{[\beta]=\left[\mathrm{MLT}^{-2}\right]}
\end{array}
$

Since, $P$ is also a dimensionless quantity.

$
\begin{aligned}
&\frac{[\alpha]}{[\beta]}=\left[\mathrm{M}^{0} \mathrm{~L}^{0} \mathrm{~T}^{0}\right] \\\\
